+## Access control
+
+By default any program on the machine, and any web page open in a browser on it, can send
+requests to the server. To restrict that:
+
+* `--api-key <key>` (or the `SD_API_KEY` environment variable, which keeps the key out of the
+  process list) makes every request need `Authorization: Bearer <key>`; others get `401`.
+  CORS preflight (`OPTIONS`) requests still get their `204`.
+* `--reject-origin` refuses every request that carries an `Origin` header with `403` and sends no
+  CORS headers, so web pages can't use the server at all. API clients (curl, Python, other apps)
+  don't send `Origin` and are unaffected. The built-in web UI doesn't work in this mode.
+
